---
---
<section id="faq" class="section">
  <div class="container-tool max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="h-section text-center mb-10">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <dl class="space-y-3">
      {[
        { q: 'Is my YAML data safe? Does it get uploaded?', a: 'No. Everything runs entirely in your browser using client-side JavaScript. Your data is never transmitted to any server — disconnect from the internet after loading and it keeps working.' },
        { q: 'Can I convert YAML to JSON with this tool?', a: 'Yes. Click the YAML to JSON tab above the editor to convert your document to formatted JSON. Nested objects, arrays, and complex structures convert without data loss.' },
        { q: 'Can I convert YAML to TOML?', a: 'Yes. Switch to the YAML to TOML tab to convert your document to TOML. Nested mappings become [table] sections, object arrays become [[array.of.tables]], and strings are quoted correctly. TOML has no null literal, so null values are omitted.' },
        { q: 'How do I convert JSON back to YAML?', a: 'Switch to the JSON to YAML tab, paste your JSON, and get clean block-style YAML instantly. Strings that could be misread — like "yes" or "8080" — are quoted automatically so values round-trip exactly.' },
        { q: 'Is the conversion accurate?', a: 'Yes. The parser follows the YAML 1.2 specification, so data types, nesting, and values are preserved exactly — the conversion is lossless.' },
        { q: 'Does it support YAML anchors and aliases?', a: 'Yes. The parser fully supports YAML 1.2 anchors (&), aliases (*), and merge keys (<<). Both the references and the resolved values are preserved in the output.' },
        { q: 'How do I expand YAML anchors and aliases?', a: 'Tick the "Expand anchors" checkbox in the Format tab. Anchors (&), aliases (*), and merge keys (<<) are resolved into their full values, so you can see exactly what your tooling receives without manually tracing references.' },
        { q: 'What happens to YAML comments during conversion?', a: 'Comments are dropped when converting to JSON, because JSON has no comment syntax. When formatting YAML without converting, comments are preserved in place.' },
        { q: 'How are YAML data types mapped to JSON?', a: 'Strings, numbers, booleans, and null map directly. YAML sequences become JSON arrays, mappings become objects, and dates become ISO 8601 strings. See the type mapping table above.' },
        { q: 'Why do some strings come out quoted?', a: 'Values that look like booleans in older YAML dialects — yes, no, on, off — or that read as numbers are quoted so the YAML parses back to the original string. It keeps round-trips exact.' },
        { q: 'Can I format multiple YAML documents at once?', a: 'Yes. Files with multiple documents separated by --- are processed independently, and the separators are preserved — useful for multi-resource Kubernetes manifests.' },
        { q: 'Does it preserve comments when formatting?', a: 'Yes. Comments keep their position relative to the surrounding keys and values during formatting.' },
        { q: 'Can I convert large files?', a: 'Yes — thousands of lines convert in moments, entirely client-side. Drag and drop .yaml, .yml, or .json files straight into the editor.' },
        { q: 'Is this YAML formatter free?', a: 'Yes, completely free with no limits. No sign-up, no usage caps. The project is open source and will stay free.' },
        { q: 'Can I use this tool offline?', a: 'Yes. Once the page is loaded, all processing happens locally in your browser. Disconnect from the internet and the formatter continues to work.' },
      ].map(({ q, a }) => (
        <div class="border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden bg-white">
          <dt>
            <button type="button" class="faq-toggle flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-4 text-left text-sm font-medium text-zinc-900 hover:bg-zinc-50" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>{q}</span>
              <svg class="faq-chevron w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
            </button>
          </dt>
          <dd class="faq-answer hidden px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">{a}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq-toggle').forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const dd = btn.closest('div')?.querySelector('.faq-answer');
      const chevron = btn.querySelector('.faq-chevron');
      const isOpen = btn.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
      btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!isOpen));
      if (dd) dd.classList.toggle('hidden');
      if (chevron) chevron.classList.toggle('rotate-180');
    });
  });
</script>